---
import Layout from "../layouts/layout.astro";
---

<Layout
    title="About | Gabby"
    description="About Gabriele Naseviciute, a senior graphic designer and creative technologist."
>
    <section class="page-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>

        <h1>Designer with a growing obsession with technology.</h1>

        <p>
            I'm Gabby, a senior graphic designer with more than 11 years of
            experience across visual communication, digital design and web.
        </p>

        <p>
            I'm now expanding that experience into Python, AI and software
            development, with a particular interest in creative technology and
            practical AI systems.
        </p>
    </section>

    <div class="about-sections">
        <section class="about-section">
            <h2>What I do</h2>
            <div class="about-section-body">
                <h3>Design</h3>
                <p>
                    I take complicated, wordy things like brand guidelines and policy
                    documents and make them clear, engaging and a pleasure to read. After 11
                    years working across platforms, I know the shortcuts, and I know how to
                    deliver work with real depth without losing efficiency. My favourite
                    briefs are the ones that look dry on the surface.
                </p>

                <h3>Technology</h3>
                <p>
                    My first line of code was a tweak to a WordPress footer, because the
                    spacing bothered me. It took a lot of Googling, and by the end I
                    thought: this isn't that hard. Now I'm building a locally hosted AI agent
                    that drafts site-specific planning documents in a company's tone, using
                    a library of past precedents. Being a designer helps: I know what the
                    person on the other side of the screen needs, and I care how the finished
                    thing looks.
                </p>
                <p>
                    I think design should stay with designers and AI should take the jobs
                    nobody likes doing. For designers, it's one of the most useful tools in
                    years.
                </p>

            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="about-section">
            <h2>Skills and tools</h2>
            <div class="about-section-body">
                <h3>Design</h3>
                <ul class="about-list">
                    <li>[Your design tools and disciplines]</li>
                </ul>

                <h3>Code</h3>
                <ul class="about-list">
                    <li>HTML, CSS and JavaScript</li>
                    <li>Astro</li>
                    <li>Git and GitHub</li>
                    <li>[Python and anything else you want to list]</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="about-section">
            <h2>Experience</h2>
            <div class="about-section-body">
                <p>[A short summary of your career so far.]</p>
                <!-- CV download link goes here once the PDF is ready -->
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="about-section">
            <h2>Contact</h2>
            <div class="about-section-body">
                <ul class="about-list">
                    <li>[Email]</li>
                    <li>[LinkedIn]</li>
                    <li>
                        <a href="https://github.com/just-gabby">GitHub</a>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </section>
    </div>
</Layout>